  "body": "## What changed\n\nM7.3 step 2/6 (#26 umbrella, split in https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/26#issuecomment-6754685656).\n\nLaw (d)'s prior-stock readers, `verify::prior_surface` and `verify::acquit_by_prior`, took `&Dexel`, which names the column engine directly. They now take `&Columns<'_>`, the M7.3 column seam that a column or field `Stock` already answers through.\n\n- **`Columns` gains `Columns::of_grid(&Dexel)`:** a borrowed bare rest grid, read through the same seam. The reader's source becomes an internal `Source::{Grid, Field}`, so a reader no longer needs a whole `Stock`.\n- **`Columns` gains `cell()`, `center(ix, iy)` and `origin()`.**\n- **The operation layer** (`drill_prior::PriorRead::surface`, `generate.rs`'s acquittal) still holds the program-ahead grid as a `Dexel`, so it wraps it with `of_grid`. #586 moves that holder onto `Stock`, and the call then becomes `stock.columns()?`.\n- **Scope corrected from the research:** `solid_rest` names no `Dexel`. `carry::Body` uses `Dexel` as storage, not as a reader, so that move goes with #586/#589. It's recorded on #585 and in `docs/decisions/585-prior-readers-on-columns.md`.\n\nThe change is behaviour-neutral: `Columns` maps a point to its column by the column engine's own formula, so a grid read through it answers identically.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **The existing `verify::prior` unit tests pass unchanged, 4/4**, wrapped in `Columns::of_grid`.\n- **New `crates/sim/tests/prior_columns.rs`, 2/2:**\n  - `the_prior_surface_reads_alike_through_a_grid_and_a_field`: inside the hole, across its rim and on the raw top, the column and field stocks agree within 1e-6. It reads the hole floor at 15 and the raw top at 25.\n  - `a_dive_is_acquitted_alike_on_either_engine_and_through_a_bare_grid`: a column stock, a field stock and a bare grid acquit the same dive and keep the same conviction.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`** escalated to batch. geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion and app all pass, and clippy `-D warnings` is clean on every crate. The only reds are the 3 headless-GPU ui tests, which are environmental on this host.\n- **Named:** drill_prior 12, drill_reach 6, carried_verify 8, setup_carry 9, stock_columns 3.\n- No golden or snapshot changed. Branched from v0.16.0, which the fork's main is synced to.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNothing user-visible changes, so there is no GUI or machine check.\n\nChangelog: none (internal refactor, behaviour-neutral)\n\nFixes #585\nRefs #26\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
